# Source-distribution contents.
#
# The published sdist used to carry 9 of the repo's test modules and none of
# the machinery that runs them - no conftest.py, no tests/__init__.py, no
# tests/fuzz/, no tests/simulator/ - because setuptools' default sdist
# heuristic picks up top-level *.py files and stops. `pytest` in the unpacked
# artifact therefore collected nothing and errored on
# `from tests.conftest import ...`.
#
# Every security fix in rounds 1-9 is asserted by a test, and the fuzz suite
# that reaches the round-8 decode shapes lives in tests/fuzz/. A downstream
# packager, an auditor, or a distribution's build system takes the *sdist* -
# so advertising a suite it cannot execute is worse than shipping none
# (round-9 security informational 1). This ships the whole thing: with the
# `dev` extra installed (which is what the shipped `addopts = "-n auto"`
# needs), `pytest` in the unpacked sdist runs the same suite CI does.
#
# `.github/workflows/test.yml`'s `packaging` job unpacks the built sdist and
# asserts this choice, so it cannot drift back silently.
graft tests
graft docs
# `tests/test_gaps_report.py` imports it by path, and it is inside the
# coverage gate, so the sdist is only self-consistent with it.
graft scripts
include CHANGELOG.md
include uv.lock

# Nothing generated, cached, or internal.
global-exclude *.py[cod]
global-exclude .coverage*
prune tests/__pycache__
prune .hypothesis
prune .claude
